{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"34a32ddbd1eb2e41382f062d081670eeab9a151519a72afb8727af3e6a20b988","digest":{"component_or_area":"test autodeploy review drain","key_entities":["tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py","box fixture","os.environ","pytest saferepr","DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX","HEALTH_TIMEOUT","PATH","test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_materialize_probe.py","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets.py","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_health_gate.py","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py","tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py","tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py"],"problem_keywords":["credential leak","pytest fixture","environment variables","test failure rendering","security","ambient secrets"],"propositions":["The box fixture copies the full os.environ dict and returns it, causing pytest default traceback rendering to print ambient credential values in test failure output.","Pytest saferepr with 240-character truncation renders fixture arguments in the failure header, exposing credentials that appear early in the environment mapping.","The fix passes only stubbed PATH and explicit test-owned variables (DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX, HEALTH_TIMEOUT) instead of full os.environ, preventing credential exposure while preserving subprocess behavior.","Seven sibling test fixtures use the same dict(os.environ)-inside-returned-fixture pattern and require identical repairs.","The nested pytest oracle test verifies that synthetic sentinel secrets no longer appear in pytest failure output after the fix."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"